# gdnav: realistic navigation for the GNSS-denied experiments
# Real EKF3 instead of the simulator-truth AHRS (type 10), otherwise losing GPS would change nothing.
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
EK3_ENABLE 1
# GPS1 = simulated GNSS receiver (gets jammed). GPS2 = visual localizer via MAVLink GPS_INPUT: it is enabled
# in flight by sim/visual_gps.py (GPS2_TYPE 14), because a nadir camera cannot localize on the ground and an
# unhealthy GPS2 would block arming.
GPS1_TYPE 1
GPS2_TYPE 0
GPS_AUTO_SWITCH 1
GPS_PRIMARY 0
# Airspeed sensor (every real fixed-wing has a pitot tube). The stock Gazebo Zephyr config disables it, which
# makes GNSS-denied dead reckoning unrealistically poor. SITL derives it from the JSON velocity (no wind support).
ARSPD_TYPE 100
ARSPD_USE 1
# Visual GPS supplies POSITION only. Its finite-difference velocity is too noisy on real imagery: the EKF used
# it to estimate wind (GPS velocity - airspeed), learned a fake wind and diverged as soon as fixes paused.
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 0
EK3_SRC1_VELZ 0
